.TH SYS_MODULES 2
.SH NAME
sys_modules \- the boot modules' names, for the supervisor (SYS_MODULES)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "mk.h"

long sys_modules(char *buf, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys_modules
copies into
.I buf
the names of the programs loaded with the kernel (the boot modules), one
after the other, each ended by a 0 byte, in order: "init\e0con\e0vblk\e0...".
A module's place in the list is its number for
.B SPAWN_MODULE
.RB ( sys_spawn (2));
number 0 is the supervisor itself.
.PP
Only the supervisor,
.BR init (8),
may call it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes copied, or a negative error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller is not the supervisor.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I size
is too small for all the names.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
is not writable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_spawn (2),
.BR init (8),
.BR boot (7)
